'''Hatsun Agro Product Ltd''', often referred to as '''Hatsun''' or '''HAP''', is an Indian private sector [[dairy]] company, headquartered in [[Chennai]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/announcements/others/shifting-of-registered-office-within-local-limits-of-the-city/article4209440.ece|title=Shifting of Registered Office within local limits of the City|work=Business Line|location=Chennai|accessdate=22 February 2015}}</ref> It was founded by [[R. G. Chandramogan]] in 1970.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/strong-sales-push-hatsun-agro-net-up/article3750998.ece|title=Strong sales push Hatsun Agro net up|work=Business Line|location=Chennai|date=10 August 2012 |accessdate=22 February 2015}}</ref>

It also exports dairy ingredient products to overseas markets.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/opinion/private-sectors-white-revolution/article4313042.ece|title=Private sector's White Revolution|first=R.G.|last=Chandramogan|work=Business Line|location=Chennai|date=16 January 2013 |accessdate=22 February 2015}}</ref>

In 2025, it acquired [[Bhubaneswar]]-based [[Milk Mantra]] for {{INRconvert|233|c}}.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tejonmayam |first1=U |title=Hatsun Agro acquires Milk Mantra |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/hatsun-agro-acquires-milk-mantra/articleshow/117646328.cms |access-date=3 September 2025 |work=The Times of India |date=28 January 2025}}</ref>

